id: pm-gh1456
title: "GH-1456: Discoverable SDK-backed bulk creation with JSONL and keyed upsert"
description: "Extend the shipped atomic SDK/CLI mutation primitive with a discoverable bulk-create workflow, JSONL input and optional keyed upsert. The existing pm item mutate surface already commits ordered create/update/close batches and must be reused rather than reimplemented."
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: agent-ux,"area:cli","area:sdk",bulk-mutations,github-intake
created_at: "2026-10-13T18:12:30.417Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-16T11:37:24.854Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-16T11:37:23.593Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-16T11:37:23.593Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: Document and execute the existing atomic create batch as the immediate recovery; Any create-many adapter delegates to public SDK transaction primitives; JSONL/ref resolution and keyed upsert preserve input order and validate before persistence; Interrupted or repeated imports preserve complete history and stable idempotency
parent: pm-n7rr
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "SDK-first bulk creation validates JSON/JSONL documents and direct batch uniqueness, preserves wrapped IDs and stable references, guards selected keys under the actual item lock, and rejects reference cycles involving matched upserts. CLI input selection distinguishes explicit flags from preserved parser defaults; MCP rejects malformed mutation arrays before planning. Private canonical key comparison returns zero for equal strings. SDK documentation distinguishes committed-plan replay from changes that produce transaction_plan_mismatch. Agent, command and SDK guides consistently require the original transaction identity and unchanged committed plan; fully compensated attempts may accept a new plan."
expected_result: "Bulk identities, uniqueness, diagnostics and match preconditions remain consistent through SDK, CLI and MCP without partial writes."
actual_result: "Build and documentation link gate pass after documentation-only corrections. Runtime and tests are unchanged from head 94345b4, whose 26 required hosted checks passed with 100/100/100/100 source coverage and zero bounded-mutation timeouts. Final documentation/metadata head requires renewed full review and its own hosted checks."
